<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>FitBuddy - Project Documentation</title>
  <style>
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f8fafc;
      color: #1e293b;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    header {
      background: #0f766e;
      color: white;
      padding: 25px 15px;
      text-align: center;
    }
    main {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 25px auto;
      padding: 0 15px;
    }
    section {
      background: white;
      padding: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 10px #0001;
    }
    h2 { color: #0f766e; }
    button {
      padding: 11px 16px;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 7px;
      background: #0f766e;
      color: white;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    footer {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 20px;
      color: #64748b;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>FitBuddy</h1>
    <p>Phase 6: Project Documentation</p>
    <p>AI-Assisted Fitness Planning Project</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section>
      <h2>1. Abstract</h2>
      <p>FitBuddy is a student project designed to help users
      explore fitness goals and view suitable workout suggestions.
      It aims to provide a simple and user-friendly interface.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Objectives</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide an easy-to-use fitness interface.</li>
        <li>Allow users to select fitness preferences.</li>
        <li>Display relevant sample workout suggestions.</li>
        <li>Explore future AI-based plan generation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Technologies Used</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>HTML – webpage structure</li>
        <li>CSS – page design</li>
        <li>JavaScript – interactive features</li>
        <li>Python and Gemini API – planned AI integration</li>
        <li>GitHub – source code management</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Project Modules</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Ideation</li>
        <li>Requirement Analysis</li>
        <li>Project Design</li>
        <li>Project Planning</li>
        <li>Project Development</li>
        <li>Project Documentation</li>
        <li>Project Demonstration</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Testing</h2>
      <p>The sample interface can be tested by selecting different
      fitness goals and checking the displayed suggestions.
      Further testing is needed when the backend and AI integration
      are implemented.</p>
      <button onclick="showTesting()">View Test Checklist</button>
      <div id="testingResult" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Future Enhancements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Integrate Gemini AI through a secure backend.</li>
        <li>Add user accounts and saved plans.</li>
        <li>Improve accessibility and mobile support.</li>
        <li>Include appropriate safety guidance.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Conclusion</h2>
      <p>FitBuddy demonstrates the design of a simple fitness
      planning application. Additional development and testing
      can expand its capabilities.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>FitBuddy Student Project</footer>

  <script>
    function showTesting() {
      document.getElementById("testingResult").innerHTML =
        "<ul>" +
        "<li>Check all page sections.</li>" +
        "<li>Test fitness goal selection.</li>" +
        "<li>Verify layout on mobile screens.</li>" +
        "<li>Check links and buttons.</li>" +
        "</ul>";
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
